{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Operator decision (2026-08-19): APPROVED — THREAD the captured values through; do not drop the capture.\n\nThread comment_max_chars and jira_cli_timeout from ReconcilerSettings into the built backend and the DC sanitizer, so the DC comment sanitizer stops calling resolve_comment_max_chars() ambiently and uses the compose-captured value instead.\n\nRationale: the two options cost about the same to implement, so cost is not the tiebreaker. Dropping the capture would preserve an ambient global read and revert a deliberate design direction — operation-scoped configuration — that the RP work is actively moving toward. Threading completes that design for these two fields; dropping it re-opens a seam that was intentionally closed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787173861883127001,"uuid":"c609b1ed-3fc4-4903-b764-350bcb6a9a1a"}